@ 10.3.3 - Proto-Oceanic to Lemerig
# citation: thetha, from François, Alexander (2005), “Unraveling the history of the vowels of
# 			seventeen north Vanuatu languages”
	p pʷ k q > β w ɣ ∅
	VV > V
	ndr *R > d r
	{c,*j} ɲ > s n
	t > ʔ
	b bʷ d ɡ > p kpʷ t k
	mʷ > ŋmʷ
	# thetha says “intervening consonants sometimes optional in the [following] sound
	# 			changes”:
	iCV:[- high] > aC
	eCV:[+ mid] > ɛC
	eCV:[+ low] > aC
	aCV:[+ high] > {ɛ,œ}C
	aCa > {ɘ,a}C
	oCV:[+ high] > øC
	— oCo > œC
	oCV:[- high] > ɔC
	uCV:[- high] > oC
	o e > ʊ ɪ
	ia > ɪ “(only somoetimes?)”
	V > ∅ / #_C”V
	V > ∅ / CVC_C”V
	CV₁C”V₂ > CV₂C”V₂